<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.00000;0.01307;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">01/12  |  WELCOME ABOARD</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Welcome aboard our spacecraft.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.01307;0.04793;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">01/12  |  WELCOME ABOARD</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Through the window on the right, we can see planet Earth floating below us.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.04793;0.08715;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">01/12  |  WELCOME ABOARD</text><text x="500" y="558" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">This dashboard monitors the cabin in real time and shows how fire safety works</tspan><tspan x="500" dy="20">in space.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.08715;0.10458;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">02/12  |  FIRE IN MICROGRAVITY</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Fire prevention is critical in space.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.10458;0.13943;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">02/12  |  FIRE IN MICROGRAVITY</text><text x="500" y="558" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">On Earth, hot gases rise because of gravity, which gives flames their teardrop</tspan><tspan x="500" dy="20">shape.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.13943;0.17211;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">02/12  |  FIRE IN MICROGRAVITY</text><text x="500" y="558" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">In microgravity, that upward motion disappears, so flames and smoke behave</tspan><tspan x="500" dy="20">very differently.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.17211;0.19826;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">03/12  |  THE ENERGY CORE</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">The glowing sphere in the center is the energy core.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.19826;0.22222;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">03/12  |  THE ENERGY CORE</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">It is a conceptual model of a spherical flame.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.22222;0.25490;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">03/12  |  THE ENERGY CORE</text><text x="500" y="558" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Without buoyancy-driven convection, heat and oxygen spread evenly in every</tspan><tspan x="500" dy="20">direction around it.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.25490;0.28540;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">04/12  |  OXYGEN CONTROL</text><text x="500" y="558" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Oxygen supports combustion, so its concentration and pressure must be</tspan><tspan x="500" dy="20">carefully monitored.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.28540;0.30937;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">04/12  |  OXYGEN CONTROL</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">The blue bubbles marked O2 remind us of this.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.30937;0.33333;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">04/12  |  OXYGEN CONTROL</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Oxygen must never be treated as a fire-suppressing gas.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.33333;0.36166;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">05/12  |  MATERIAL SELECTION</text><text x="500" y="558" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">We reduce fire risks by selecting approved materials with controlled</tspan><tspan x="500" dy="20">flammability.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.36166;0.38998;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">05/12  |  MATERIAL SELECTION</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Every item brought on board is tested against strict safety standards.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.38998;0.41830;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">05/12  |  MATERIAL SELECTION</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Fewer flammable materials means fewer ways for a fire to start.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.41830;0.44444;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">06/12  |  ELECTRICAL SAFETY</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Electrical equipment is one of the most common ignition sources.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.44444;0.46405;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">06/12  |  ELECTRICAL SAFETY</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Cables, batteries, and connections are inspected regularly.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.46405;0.50109;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">06/12  |  ELECTRICAL SAFETY</text><text x="500" y="558" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">Damaged wiring and overheating components can become serious hazards if they</tspan><tspan x="500" dy="20">are not detected early.</tspan></text></g>
<g opacity="0"><animate attributeName="opacity" values="0;1;0;0" keyTimes="0.00000;0.50109;0.53595;1.00000" calcMode="discrete" dur="210s" repeatCount="indefinite"/><text x="116" y="540" fill="#53DFFF" font-size="10" font-weight="700">07/12  |  SMOKE BEHAVIOR</text><text x="500" y="566" fill="#F2FAFF" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="500" dy="0">In microgravity, smoke does not rise toward the ceiling as it does on Earth.</tspan></text></g>
